I started an Archeologist, because I wanted to play a "cuisinart" as a friend
described double-weilding silver sabers.  I ended up with Z, female human A,
who ascended Wishless, Genoless, Polyselfless.

Thanks to the help when I had my New Moon Disaster (mentioned below).

Oh, this is kinda long; you've been warned ;-)  And of course, spoily and
full of neat hints (at least *I* think so, and hey, I ascended!)

Early game went fairly well.  An early bones file netted standard wizard
stuff, and a pet dog called "MINE!!!!!!!".  My original pet turned
into a cockatrice (via a trap or wand, forget which), as I recall...which
was fun for a while, but I got bored (they're slow, and don't attack big
monsters, and I didn't have conflict).  So I polymorphed it into a Water
Troll, and MINE!!!!! became an L (this time, I'm sure it was a wand).

About this time, I had my New Moon almost disaster (see YA New Moon
Disaster).  I had seen no lizards, got too close to a c, and only
divine intervention saved me (I waited 'till after the new moon was over
before trying to pray!)  Stupid stupid stupid!

I wandered about a bit, found reflection in Sokoban (I forget where I got
my bag of holding), and found a cross-aligned temple on DL11 - the
entrance to the quest was there too!  And on the level below was the
portal to Ludos.  Suddenly, I'm thinking "Oooooh - good place for a temple
to Quetzalcoatl!"  But there's this annoying priest in the way, and it
turns out that L's, while great at killing shopkeepers, are terrible
against Priests, who tend to resist their attack!  So, out comes the wand
of PolyMorph, and a hunt for suitable pets!  I think I had lost the water
troll somehow, which was a bummer, because I think he'd have taken on the
priest ok.  Eventually, I picked up a second L, which I felt compelled to
name "YOURS!!!!!!" and Kitty, who turned into a Bone Devil.  Yay!  Kitty
was *quite* happy to help the good cause along!

As a side note, an L can take out a priest, it just takes a *loooong*
time...I'm guessing it's some sort of magic cancellation going on, because
every once in a while, they'd hurt the priest.  It just wasn't fast enough
for me :-/

So, I moved my stashs from Sokoban and level 3 to the new Temple, and
proceeded to sacrifice. I got (in no particular order):
Snickersnee
Fire Brand
Dragonbane
Sunsword

Eventually, I enchanged Snickersnee up to +5, but at some point, I finally
got Grayswandir, and Snickersnee got relagated to the chest, after Kitty
wouldn't weild it.  I eventually gave her Fire Brand.  (I'm guessing it's
because it's a Lawful artifact?)

The quest was a pushover (double-weilding chop chop chop chop chop) - I
don't think the Minion got more then one move...

I had all the major intrinsics after the quest...except disintigration,
which I wasn't too worried about.

Medusa was DL26, and may have had the Titan (I don't remember seeing it
much, maybe my L killed it?  Anyway, it'd've been peaceful, so of no
consequence). MINE!!!!!! got turned into stone by Medusa...  I don't know
what possesses Ls to attack Medusa...  Kitty at least had an extra amulet
of reflection, but MINE!!!! was not so equipped.  I left her statue as a
monument to ...something, not sure what. When I came back later with Stone
To Flesh, I thought about reviving the statue, but wasn't sure it'd be
tame, so I just left it there.

Castle had 2 Gray Dragons, and 2 Silver dragons, and all of a sudden, I'm
thinking, Ooooooo - scale mail!  I hacked them to bits many many times (I
had a wand of undead turning), but eventually got bored, when nothing
happened.  I was thinking about going wishless, but really wanted Scale
Mail, and was at the point of saying, "The Hell with it!"  So I get out of
the corridore-o-trapdoors, and go to kill the last gray D that had
wandered in here...and he gives me scales!  At that point, I decide, "I'm
not even going to go get the wand of wishing!"  I had also decided not the
genocide anything; I had had two pet Ls at that point.  So, some conducts
for me :-)

This was the first game that I know of where I wasn't invisible.  I had a
cloak of displacement, and it's really really nice!  Although it does have
a few...downsides.  Asmodeus tried talking to my displaced figure...and
when I didn't answer his whispers, he got angry.  He eventually ran to the
upstairs, and I just walked away from him...

Orcus got off one shot w/ his wand of death before falling to the
double-silvered might that was Z.  At this point, I had 3 wands of death!

When I finally found where the Wizard was, I decided to take my loot back
up to my temple and try to polypile for some good rings/scrolls/etc.  On
the way back up, I ran into Asmodeus again, whom I'd *completely*
forgotten about.  In a bit of sillyness, he kept running away, and I kept
chasing him.  Eventually, I wondered how far it'd go, so I follewed him
all the way to DL1 (killing Dispater off in the process).  Alas, he
wouldn't flee out of the dungeon!  So I killed him.

Long story short:
Wore a ring of Slow digestion for most of the rest of the game.
Polypiled in Ludos, found VS, polypiled some more...never got a =oFreeAction.
Oh well!
Did get a T-shirt "Is that Mjollnir in your pocket, or are you happy to
see me?" which I managed to enchant to +5.
Kitty died somewhere in Gehennom :-(

Confused "Remove Curse" to get Unholy Water...And nurse danced to 281 hph.

Decked myself out w/ cursed scrolls of teleport, about 15 uncursed scrolls
of T, 5 potions of Gain Level...cursed, and alchemised up to 561 hp.  (!) 
I still had a handfull for the ascention run, too!  I also blanked a bunch
of potions of Gain Ability to get water, and realized afterwards that I no
longer wanted to polymorph to eat rings, because if my stats lowered, I
couldn't raise them.  Oh well.

Spells of Note:
Magic Missle (didn't use so much)
Detect Treasure, Detect Monsters, Magic Mapping
  (makes looting Gehennom *easy*)
Cure Disease 0%, Healing, Extra Healing
Fireball, Cone of Cold, Drain Life (used Cone of Cold like 4 times...none
  of the others)
Stone to Flesh

Level-ported down to where Wizard was, and pulled off a neat trick.  I'd
found a statue of a cockatrice in one of the mazes, and lugged it back up.
So when I got there, I StoneToFleshed it, killed it...and it left a
corpse!

I get to the zoo upstairs, and reduce half the occupants to a statue
garden, then run on through to the Wizard.  I get there (turning the ;
into underwater statues), cross over some Ice (almost ran out of wands of
cold - only brought 1!) and make a Historical Statue of the Wizard.  After
I get his pet Hell Hound, the corpse rots away - works for me!

My pet L YOURS!!!!!! picked up the Book of the Dead; had me worried for a
bit there, but it was all good when he finally dropped it.

Level-ported down to DL49, did the ritual, and then level ported down to
DL50 (a trick I saw on rgrn); I ended up just outside the sanctum!  I also
ended up surrounded by 4 angry priests...  I burned through my 3 scrolls
of taming here, and did get a purple worm for my trouble (who died very
quickly - never saw what got it...), and a few other beasts who got left
behind...  Used a /oSecred Door Detection to get into the sanctum, offed
the priest with a wand of death, named the Amulet W00t!, and the run was
on!  Two cursed potions of gain level later, I'm on DL48 and moving.

Run went very quickly - I'd dug out enough passageways to make traversal
very quick. On levels where > and < were far apart, I used scrolls of
teleportation; when I got thrown back to a far corner of the dungeon, I'd
use !oGL (and I used my last one the second time I left Juiblex's swamp -
that's the *fast* way to cross that swamp!)  Never saw the Wizard, never
summoned nasties, may have gotten black aura once...maybe.  I stopped at
my cache to pick up extra stuff, and was on my way!

I used confused scrolls of Gold Detection to blitz through the planes. 
But 561hp and double weilding +7 Grayswandir and +7 silver saber make
quick work of even Air elementals.  Magic mapping on Air helped, too, and
Detect Monsters was golden!

Took me a bit to find the portal on Water...ran out of scrolls, and
discovered that using the Orb of Detection would put me in a trace for so
long that the portal would move halfway across the map before I could get
where I'd seen it :-/  Eventually stumbled across it, and left Water w/o
my V - only YOURS!!!!! came along.  (Next time, I'll use the Orb on the 
*other* planes, and save scrolls for water.)

When I arried, I saw that Death was coming at me from the Right already,
so I figured I might as well get it out of the way.  He never managed to
hit me :-) Right was Neutral - drat!

Middle was Famine, and since I had *plenty* of food..and Famine was again
already out the door coming at me, I went that way.  Ran into a bit of
excitement when an evil Archeologist snapped Grayswandir out of my hands! 
I burned half a dozen shots from my Wands of Death and never hit him...I
finally shot him w/ a wand of sleep...only to discover that he had on
SDSM.  Figures.  Thankfully, I'd lugged Snickersnee up here (at +5), so I
managed to hack him to pieces and recover Grayswandir.  Alas, middle altar
was Chaotic.  

I had a helm of opposite alignment, but figured that nothing was really
hurting me (yet), and I still had lots of !oFH and Cure Disease at 0%, 
so I'd head over to take on Pestilance.  Again, never got hit (did I 
mention that Displacement rocks?), fought my way into the temple, cleaned
it out, called in my pets (first time I've *ever* kept my guardian angel
alive), and...

